ose labels. The age split is under 25 versus 25 and older, which is a reporting choice. Age is an input to the model, and personal status is an input to the benchmark model. A cell with few defaults moves when one or two people change outcome. This is not a fair-lending review, not a U.S. applicant population, and not a reason by itself to approve or deny anyone."
